  <clipboard-copy role="menuitem" value="Hi @arthw - 
I&#39;ve rebased this onto master (4f92965a7) and added a fix so MXFP4 experts are reordered before the multi-token per-expert loop.

Previously, the reorder only happened in the fused single-token decode path. That meant the first set of prompt-processing tests ran before the experts were reordered, while later tests used the reordered layout. Swapping -fa 0,1 to -fa 1,0 confirmed that the pp results depended on which mode ran first.

With the fix, I’m seeing roughly 20–33% higher pp throughput on my Arc Pro B70 with gpt-oss-20b-Q8_0 (in this unsloth file the expert tensors are MXFP4), in both FA modes and both test orders. Decode improves by about 13–16% with FA off and roughly doubles with FA on. Both builds (stock master and this PR) pass all MUL_MAT_ID and MUL_MAT backend tests, and the perplexity results are within the reported uncertainty.

The rebase also picks up the corrected Metal fusion test baseline from #29812, which should address the earlier CI failure.
This is ready to retest on your A770. I can confirm the order-dependent behavior on the B70, but I can’t verify the earlier 10% pp drop on your hardware here. 

Please give the updated version another run with both FA settings when you have a chance." data-view-component="true" class="dropdown-item btn-link">
      
