          <p dir="auto">Hi <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/arthw/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/arthw">@arthw</a> -<br>
I've rebased this onto master (<a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/4f92965a7bfa9e8eb6519908ff962e23c2cb7b93/hovercard" href="https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/commit/4f92965a7bfa9e8eb6519908ff962e23c2cb7b93"><tt>4f92965</tt></a>) and added a fix so MXFP4 experts are reordered before the multi-token per-expert loop.</p>
<p dir="auto">Previously, the reorder only happened in the fused single-token decode path. That meant the first set of prompt-processing tests ran before the experts were reordered, while later tests used the reordered layout. Swapping -fa 0,1 to -fa 1,0 confirmed that the pp results depended on which mode ran first.</p>
<p dir="auto">With the fix, I’m seeing roughly 20–33% higher pp throughput on my Arc Pro B70 with gpt-oss-20b-Q8_0 (in this unsloth file the expert tensors are MXFP4), in both FA modes and both test orders. Decode improves by about 13–16% with FA off and roughly doubles with FA on. Both builds (stock master and this PR) pass all MUL_MAT_ID and MUL_MAT backend tests, and the perplexity results are within the reported uncertainty.</p>
<p dir="auto">The rebase also picks up the corrected Metal fusion test baseline from <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5665523371" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/29812" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/29812/hovercard" href="https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/29812">#29812</a>, which should address the earlier CI failure.<br>
This is ready to retest on your A770. I can confirm the order-dependent behavior on the B70, but I can’t verify the earlier 10% pp drop on your hardware here.</p>
<p dir="auto">Please give the updated version another run with both FA settings when you have a chance.</p>

